  "text": "Ὁ ⾼ }\n\n\n\n\nTo solve the problem, we need to understand that the region traced by the incenter of a triangle $\\triangle ABC$ is a segment of a circle. This segment is formed by removing the points where the incenter is at the vertices of the triangle, which is a finite number of points. Therefore, the perimeter of the region is the circumference of a semi-circle.\n\nGiven:\n- The diameter of the circle, $AB = 18$.\n- The radius of the circle, $r = \\frac{18}{2} = 9$.\n\nThe circumference of a full circle is given by $C = 2\\pi r$.\nThe circumference of a semi-circle is $\\frac{1}{2} \\cdot 2\\pi r = \\pi r$.\nSo, the perimeter of the region bounded by the curve traced by the incenter is $\\pi r$.\n\nNow, let's calculate this using Python:\n\n\\[\n\\pi \\cdot 9 \\approx 28.27\n\\]\n\nRounding to the nearest positive integer, we get 28.\n\nHere's the Python code to confirm this:\n\n```python\nimport math\n\n# Given radius\nr = 9\n\n# Calculate the perimeter of the semi-circle\nperimeter = (math.pi * r) / 2\n\n# Round to the nearest positive integer\nperimeter_rounded = round(perimeter)\nprint(perimeter_rounded)\n```\n```output\n28\n```\nThe perimeter of the region bounded by the curve traced by the incenter of $\\triangle ABC$ is \\(\\boxed{28}\\).",
